# WAP Manager — core (never skip)

This repo is **one manager for many operators/campaigns**, not a new project per campaign.

The **main system is tracking**: one visit, every hop visible in Campaign Logs / Session Detail (`api_call_logs`). Pages are the other half: each flow type ships its own dummy funnel so create-campaign looks complete.

## 1. Logging (required on every new flow / API)

Any HTTP we send **or receive** (partner, HE, OTP, DCB, operator callback, vendor postback, internal proxy) must be persisted with **request + response** (URL, body, status, success/error).

- Use `apiCallLogService.record` (`backend/src/modules/flow/api-call-log.service.js`).
- Add a `callType` in `ApiCallType` (`api-call-log.entity.js`) if none fits (`varchar(32)`).
- Attach `visitId`, `campaignId`, `clickId`, `rcid`, `msisdn` whenever they exist. Visit is created **before** outbound HE/partner HTTP.
- Failures must still log (`success: false`, `errorMessage`, body if any). Swallowing a log write is a bug.
- Do not `console.log` a partner call and skip `api_call_logs`. If it is not in log history, it did not happen for ops.

Pattern: partner HTTP already does this in `partner-api.service.js` / `otp.service.js` / detect helpers. Copy that, do not invent a parallel logger.

Attribution (`click_id`, `rcid`, campids) stays in **our** logs; do not put it on third-party request URLs/bodies.

## 2. Dummy pages (required on every new flow type)

A flow type (e.g. `BOTH`, `OTP_ONLY`, `UNIVERSE_DCB`) is **config**, not a new app. On campaign **create**, every page in `ALL_CAMPAIGN_PAGE_TYPES` must exist with HTML that matches **that** flow — polished dummy, not a blank canvas.

- Seed HTML/CSS in `backend/src/database/seed/default-funnel-pages.js` via `getDefaultFunnelPageData(pageType, { verificationMode })`.
- Campaign create / `ensureCampaignPages` already auto-creates from that. New flow = new dummy branch there (see `UNIVERSE_DCB` HOME/OTP), not a one-off campaign patch.
- Keep frontend snippets in sync (`frontend/src/editor/utils/funnelGuide.js`) when defaults change.
- Dummies must look like a real operator funnel (layout, CTA, placeholders `{{operator}}` / `{{country}}` / packs). Empty `projectData` + no HTML is not done.

## Don't

- New operator/flow = copy-paste a second logging path or a second page seeder.
- Ship a flow whose Session Detail is missing hops, or whose new campaign pages are blank/classic-only when the mode needs different screens.
